    <li>mass-produce items from our patterns in a factory setting.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>For any other use, please <a href="/contact">ask us first</a>. We’re usually happy to help.</p>

  <h2>3. Newsletter and messages</h2>
  <p>
    When you subscribe or contact us, you confirm that the details you give are your own and accurate. You can
    unsubscribe at any time. How we handle your information is explained in our
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Accuracy of patterns</h2>
  <p>
    We test every pattern with care, but mistakes can happen. Results also depend on your yarn, hook, tension and
    experience. Patterns are provided “as is”, and we can’t guarantee that your finished item will match ours exactly. If
    you spot an error, please <a href="/contact">let us know</a> so we can fix it.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Safety</h2>
  <p>
    Take extra care with items for babies, young children and pets. Secure all parts firmly, avoid small pieces such as
    buttons or safety eyes that could come loose, and never leave a baby unsupervised with crocheted items. You are
    responsible for checking that what you make is safe for its intended use.
  </p>

